EXAMPLES = [
("how do i make a really good cup of coffee at home",
"""Start with whole beans roasted within the last few weeks and grind them just before brewing; ground coffee goes stale in minutes, not days. Use roughly one gram of coffee for every sixteen grams of water, and weigh both if you can, because a kitchen scale will improve your coffee more than any expensive machine. Heat the water to just off the boil, around 93 to 96 degrees Celsius. If the result tastes sour or thin, grind finer or brew longer; if it tastes bitter and harsh, grind coarser or brew shorter. Change one thing at a time, and within a week you'll be making coffee you'd happily pay for."""),

("how to cook rice without a rice cooker",
"""Rinse the rice in a sieve until the water runs mostly clear, which washes off surface starch and keeps the grains from turning gummy. For long-grain white rice, use about one and a half cups of water for every cup of rice. Bring it to a boil in a pot with a tight lid, add a pinch of salt, then turn the heat as low as it will go, cover, and leave it alone for fifteen minutes. Don't lift the lid; the steam is doing the work. Take it off the heat, let it rest covered for another ten minutes, then fluff it with a fork. Brown rice needs more water and roughly twice the time."""),

("how can i get better at waking up early",
"""Move your bedtime first; an early alarm without an early night is just a plan to be tired. Shift both by fifteen minutes every few days rather than all at once, and keep the same wake time on weekends, since sleeping in on Saturday quietly resets your body clock. Get bright light, ideally daylight, within the first half hour of waking, because light is the strongest signal your internal clock listens to. And give yourself something worth getting up for, even something small, like a quiet coffee before anyone else is awake. Mornings are much easier to keep when they belong to you."""),

("how should i train for my first 10k",
"""Give yourself eight to ten weeks and build gradually. Run three or four times a week, and keep most of those runs at an easy pace, one where you could hold a conversation; it will feel too slow, and that's the point. Once a week, make one run a little longer than the others, adding a kilometer or so every week or two, until it reaches about ten kilometers. Don't increase your total weekly distance by more than about ten percent at a time, since overdoing it is how most new runners get hurt. In the last week, run less, rest more, and arrive at the start line feeling slightly underused."""),

("how do i get a red wine stain out of a carpet",
"""Act quickly and blot, never rub; rubbing pushes the wine deeper into the fibers and spreads it. Press a clean cloth onto the stain to soak up as much as you can. Then pour a little cold water on it and blot again, repeating until the cloth comes up only faintly pink. For what remains, mix a tablespoon of dish soap and a tablespoon of white vinegar into two cups of warm water, dab it on, and keep blotting. Finish with plain water to rinse out the soap. Test any cleaner on a hidden corner first, especially on wool or a light-colored carpet."""),

("how do i start a vegetable garden on my balcony",
"""Begin by watching how much sun your balcony gets, because that decides everything else. Six or more hours of direct sun will support tomatoes, peppers, and most herbs; three or four hours suits lettuce, spinach, and mint. Use proper containers with drainage holes, the bigger the better, since small pots dry out within hours in summer, and fill them with potting mix rather than garden soil, which compacts in pots. Start with a few forgiving plants, such as cherry tomatoes, basil, and lettuce, and water deeply whenever the top few centimeters of soil feel dry. A small, successful first season is worth more than an ambitious one that wilts by July."""),

("how do i write a good cover letter",
"""Write it for one specific job, and assume the reader has a stack of others to get through. Open with why this role at this company interests you, in a sentence that couldn't be pasted into any other application. Then pick two or three accomplishments that match what the job asks for, and describe them concretely: what you did, and what changed because of it. Don't repeat your résumé; explain the parts of it that matter most here. Keep the whole thing under a page, end with a plain sentence saying you'd welcome a conversation, and read it aloud once before sending. Anything that sounds stiff when spoken will sound stiff on the page."""),

("how do i ask my boss for a raise",
"""Prepare as though you were making a case to someone who wants to say yes but needs a reason. Know what people in similar roles are paid, and come with a specific number. More important, gather evidence of what you've contributed: projects you led, problems you solved, responsibilities you've taken on since your pay was last set. Ask for a meeting dedicated to the conversation rather than raising it in passing, and frame it around your value and your future at the company, not your expenses. If the answer is no, ask what it would take to get to yes and when you can revisit it. A clear path is often worth almost as much as the raise itself."""),

("how do i keep a sourdough starter alive",
"""A starter is a colony of wild yeast and bacteria, and keeping it alive is mostly a matter of feeding it on a schedule. At room temperature, discard all but a few spoonfuls once a day and feed what's left with equal weights of flour and water; it should bubble and rise within several hours. If you bake less often, keep it in the fridge, where it slows down and needs feeding only about once a week. A layer of grayish liquid on top means it's hungry, not dead: pour it off and feed it. Starters are hardier than their reputation, and even a neglected one usually recovers after a few regular feedings."""),

("how do i fall asleep faster",
"""Keep your wake-up time the same every day, which steadies your body's sense of when sleep should come. In the last hour before bed, dim the lights and put the phone somewhere out of reach; bright light and endless scrolling both tell your brain it's still daytime. Keep the bedroom cool and dark. If you've been lying awake for what feels like twenty minutes, get up and do something dull in low light until you feel drowsy, so that your bed stays associated with sleep rather than frustration. And go easy on caffeine after midday: it lingers in the body far longer than most people expect."""),

("whats the best way to learn touch typing",
"""Put your fingers on the home row, with the left index finger on F and the right on J, feeling the small bumps on those keys, and commit to never looking down. That last part is the whole game. A free typing tutor website will introduce the keys a few at a time; practice for fifteen or twenty minutes a day rather than in long sessions. Aim for accuracy first and let speed come later, because errors practiced fast become habits. Expect your typing to feel slower for a couple of weeks before it becomes much faster. That dip is the sound of an old habit being replaced."""),

("how do i clean a cast iron pan",
"""Clean it while it's still warm. Rinse it under hot water and scrub with a stiff brush or a scraper; a small amount of dish soap is fine, despite the folklore, since modern soap won't strip a well-built seasoning. For stuck-on food, scrub with coarse salt and a splash of water. The two real enemies are soaking and air-drying, which invite rust. Dry the pan thoroughly with a towel, set it on a low burner for a minute to drive off the last moisture, then wipe a very thin film of oil over the surface while it's warm. Done regularly, this keeps the pan slick and makes it a little better every time you use it."""),

("how do you change a flat tire",
"""Pull well off the road onto flat, firm ground, turn on your hazard lights, and set the parking brake. Find the spare, the jack, and the lug wrench, usually under the floor of the trunk. Before lifting the car, loosen each lug nut about half a turn while the tire is still on the ground; otherwise the wheel just spins. Place the jack at the reinforced lifting point described in your owner's manual and raise the car until the flat tire clears the ground. Remove the nuts and the wheel, mount the spare, and hand-tighten the nuts. Lower the car, then tighten the nuts fully in a star pattern, alternating across the wheel. Most spares are meant only for short distances at modest speeds, so get the real tire repaired soon."""),

("how do i make friends after moving to a new city",
"""Friendship mostly grows out of repeated, low-stakes contact, so the trick is to put yourself somewhere you'll see the same people again and again. A weekly class, a running club, a choir, a volunteer shift, or a recreational sports team will do more than any number of one-off events, because the second and third meetings are where acquaintances start to become friends. When you click with someone, be the one who suggests a specific plan: coffee on Thursday, not "we should hang out sometime." It will feel forward. Almost everyone is quietly relieved when someone else makes the first move."""),

("my houseplants keep dying, what am i doing wrong",
"""The most common culprit is too much water, not too little. Roots need air as well as moisture, and soil that never dries out suffocates them and lets rot set in. Before watering, push a finger a few centimeters into the soil; if it's still damp, wait. Make sure every pot has a drainage hole and that no plant sits in a saucer of standing water. The second culprit is light: most houseplants want bright, indirect light near a window, and a plant across the room from one is living in what it experiences as dusk. Start with forgiving plants, such as pothos, snake plants, or ZZ plants, and let a few successes teach you their rhythms."""),

("how do you fold a fitted sheet",
"""Hold the sheet inside out by two adjacent corners, with a hand tucked into each corner pocket. Bring your hands together and fold one corner over the other, so the first pocket nests inside the second. Then find the other two corners and nest them the same way. You now have something like a thick, rumpled rectangle with all four corners tucked into each other. Lay it flat on a bed or table, fold the elasticated edges inward to make clean sides, and then fold it as you would any rectangle. It will never look quite as crisp as it did in the package, and that is not a personal failing."""),

("how do i stop procrastinating",
"""Procrastination is rarely laziness; it's usually a way of avoiding an unpleasant feeling, such as boredom, uncertainty, or the fear of doing something badly. So aim at the feeling, not your character. Shrink the task until starting is almost too easy to resist: not "write the report" but "open the document and write one ugly sentence." Commit to working for ten minutes, after which you're allowed to stop; most of the time, you won't want to. Remove the easiest escape, which for most people is the phone, by putting it in another room. And forgive yourself for yesterday's delays, since guilt tends to feed the very avoidance it's angry about."""),

("how should i prepare for a job interview",
"""Study the company enough to say, in your own words, what it does and why the role interests you. Then reread the job description and, for each major requirement, prepare a short story from your experience that shows you doing that thing: the situation, what you did, and how it turned out. Rehearse those stories aloud until they're crisp but not memorized. Prepare two or three thoughtful questions of your own, since an interview is also your chance to judge them. Finally, handle the logistics the day before, such as the route, the link, and the outfit, so that your attention on the day goes to the conversation."""),

("how do i say no to extra work without sounding lazy",
"""Make the no about priorities rather than effort. Something like: "I'd like to help, but taking this on would mean pushing back the launch work, which I understand to be the priority. Which would you prefer I focus on?" That shows you're thinking about the team's goals, and it hands the trade-off back to the person who can actually make it. If you can, offer a smaller alternative, such as a quick review instead of ownership, or help next month rather than now. Saying no clearly and early is far more professional than saying yes and quietly dropping something."""),

("how do i write a thank you note",
"""Keep it short, specific, and prompt. Name the gift or the kindness, then say one concrete thing about why it mattered to you: how you'll use it, what it made possible, or how it made you feel. "Thank you for the blue scarf. It has already become the thing I grab on my way out the door, and every time I do, I think of you" is worth more than a paragraph of general gratitude. Close with a warm line about the person or a hope to see them soon. Handwritten is lovely, but a prompt, sincere email beats a perfect card that never gets sent."""),

("how do i give a good toast at a wedding",
"""Keep it under three minutes and build it around one story. Introduce yourself in a sentence, then tell a short, specific anecdote that shows something true and good about the person you know, ideally something that also sheds light on why they and their partner belong together. Avoid inside jokes the room won't understand and anything that would embarrass the couple in front of their grandparents. Then turn to address both of them directly with a sincere wish, and raise your glass. Write it out, practice it aloud a few times, and bring notes. Nobody minds a card in your hand; everyone minds a speech that wanders."""),

("how do i make a budget for the first time",
"""Start by looking backward before planning forward. Go through the last two or three months of bank and card statements and sort your spending into a few broad categories: housing, food, transportation, subscriptions, and everything else. Most people are surprised by at least one of them. Then compare your monthly take-home pay with those totals. Decide in advance how much goes to fixed costs, how much to savings, ideally moved automatically on payday, and how much is free to spend. Check in once a week for a few minutes. A budget isn't a prohibition; it's a decision made calmly ahead of time, so that you don't have to make it in the checkout line."""),

("how do i get my dog to stop pulling on the leash",
"""The key is to make sure pulling never works. Whenever the leash goes tight, stop walking and stand still. The moment your dog eases back and the leash slackens, praise them and move forward again. This will make your first walks slow and a little absurd, but the dog learns quickly that a loose leash is what makes the walk continue. Reward them with small treats when they walk near your side, and practice in boring places before trying exciting ones. Consistency matters more than technique: if pulling works even occasionally, the dog will keep trying it."""),

("how do i make my apartment feel cozier",
"""Fix the lighting first; it matters more than furniture. Replace harsh overhead light with several lamps at different heights, using warm bulbs, so that the room glows in pools rather than being uniformly lit. Then add softness: a rug, a throw blanket, curtains that reach the floor, cushions you actually want to lean on. Bring in something living, even one plant, and something personal, such as books, photographs, or art you chose rather than art that came with the frame. Finally, make one corner genuinely inviting, with a chair, a lamp, and a small table for a cup. A room feels cozy when it's obviously built for someone to stay a while."""),

("how do i start journaling",
"""Lower the bar until it's almost impossible to fail. Write three sentences a night, or for five minutes, and let yourself stop there. If a blank page freezes you, use a simple prompt: what happened today, what you're thinking about, and one thing you noticed. Don't write for an imagined reader, and don't aim for good prose; the point is honesty, not polish. Keep the notebook somewhere you'll see it at the time you plan to write. After a few months, read back through it. Most people find that the ordinary days turn out to be the most interesting ones to revisit."""),

("how do i memorize a speech",
"""Don't memorize it word for word; memorize its structure. Break the speech into a handful of sections and give each one a short label, so that you hold a list of five or six ideas rather than a wall of sentences. Learn the opening and the closing lines exactly, since those are where nerves strike hardest. Then rehearse out loud and on your feet, letting the wording vary a little each time while the ideas stay in order. Practice in different rooms and at different times of day, so that your memory isn't tied to one setting. By the end, you'll know the speech the way you know a story you've told many times."""),

("how do you pick a ripe avocado",
"""Cradle it in your palm and squeeze gently, without your fingertips, which bruise the flesh. A ripe avocado yields slightly, like a firm peach; one that feels soft or has dents is past its best. Then flick off the little stem cap at the top. If it comes away easily and the spot underneath is green, the avocado is ready. If it's brown, the flesh is likely browning too. If you're buying for later in the week, choose a firm one and let it ripen on the counter. A paper bag with a banana speeds things up."""),

("how do i boil an egg perfectly",
"""Bring a pot of water to a rolling boil first, then lower the eggs in gently with a spoon. Starting them in boiling water makes the timing reliable and the eggs easier to peel. For a runny yolk, cook them for six and a half minutes; for a jammy, just-set yolk, about eight; for fully firm, eleven or twelve. The moment the timer goes, move them into a bowl of ice water for a few minutes to stop the cooking. Peel them under a thin stream of cold water, starting from the wide end, where there's a small pocket of air."""),

("how should i prepare for a long day hike",
"""Check the weather and the route the night before, and tell someone where you're going and when you expect to be back. Pack more water than you think you'll need, roughly half a liter per hour of hiking in warm weather, plus food that's easy to eat on the move. Bring a layer for warmth and one for rain even if the forecast is clear, since conditions change faster in the hills than in town. A map, a headlamp, a small first-aid kit, and sun protection round out the essentials. Wear shoes you've already broken in, start early, and set a turnaround time you'll honor whether or not you've reached the top."""),

("how can i read more books",
"""Read in the gaps you already have. Keep a book, or an e-reader, wherever you tend to wait: your bag, your nightstand, the kitchen. Replace one habitual scroll a day with ten pages, and those pages add up to a couple of dozen books a year. Give yourself permission to abandon books you aren't enjoying; life is too short, and a dull book is the fastest way to stop reading altogether. And read what you actually want to read, not what you think you should. Momentum matters more than merit, and the habit, once built, will make room for the harder books later."""),

("how do i unclog a drain without harsh chemicals",
"""Start mechanically. Remove the stopper and pull out whatever hair and gunk you can reach; a bent wire or an inexpensive plastic drain snake works wonders on bathroom sinks and showers. For a kitchen sink, try a plunger, with a few centimeters of water in the basin to make a seal. If it's still slow, pour boiling water down the drain to soften grease. The baking soda and vinegar method fizzes impressively but does little to an actual clog. If none of this works, the blockage is probably deeper in the pipe, and that's when it's worth calling a plumber."""),

("how do i learn a new language as an adult",
"""Adults can learn languages well; they just learn differently from children, with less immersion and more structure. Aim for a little every day rather than a lot once a week, because memory responds to frequent repetition. Use a spaced-repetition app to build vocabulary, but don't stop there: listen to podcasts or shows made for learners, read simple texts you find interesting, and speak as early as you can, even badly, with a tutor or a conversation partner. Expect long plateaus where nothing seems to improve. They usually end with a sudden morning when you understand far more than you did a week before."""),

("how do i take better photos with my phone",
"""Pay attention to light before anything else. Soft light, such as overcast skies, the hour after sunrise or before sunset, or a window beside your subject, flatters almost everything, while harsh midday sun creates hard shadows and squinting faces. Wipe the lens; a fingerprint smudge is behind more blurry photos than any shaky hand. Get closer than feels natural, and keep the background simple. Before you press the shutter, tap the screen to focus on your subject and drag the exposure slider down slightly, since phones tend to brighten scenes too much. And take several shots, then keep only the best one."""),

("is it possible to negotiate rent",
"""Often, yes, especially when renewing a lease or when the market is slow. Your strongest position is as a tenant the landlord wouldn't want to lose. Before your lease is up, find out what comparable apartments nearby are renting for, then write to your landlord to say you'd like to stay and ask whether they'd consider keeping the rent the same, or raising it less than proposed. Point out what makes you a good tenant: on-time payments, care for the place, a willingness to sign a longer lease. Landlords know that a vacant month and the cost of finding someone new often outweigh a modest increase."""),

("whats the easiest way to back up my computer",
"""Use two kinds of backup, because each protects against something the other doesn't. First, an automatic local backup to an external drive, using the tool built into your computer: Time Machine on a Mac or File History on Windows. Plug it in and let it run continuously. Second, an automatic cloud backup service, which protects you if the house floods or both the computer and the drive are stolen. The test of a backup is whether you can restore from it, so every few months, pick a file and try. A backup you've never tested is really just a hope."""),
]
